  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cv_image_normalize(image: list, mean: list, std: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Image Normalize** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_image_normalize(image: list, mean: list, std: list) -> list:\n    arr = np.array(image, dtype=float)\n    m = np.array(mean, dtype=float)[:, None, None]\n    s = np.array(std, dtype=float)[:, None, None]\n    return np.round((arr - m) / s, 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
